@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Chapter 6 stream shape exercise
+
+Separate public-library consumer. `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and `go build -o /tmp/ch07 .` from this directory. The example uses only the root `ensemble` package and the same actor/Engine as the core CLI. It does not interpret provider frames.
+
+Set `LLM_VENDOR`, `LLM_MODEL`, `LLM_BASE_URL`, `LLM_API_KEY`, optionally `LLM_MAX_TOKENS` and `EN_TOOL_BATCH_LIMIT`. `CH07_NO_STREAM=1` opts out independently of the core's `EN_DISABLE_STREAMING`. Input may be one plain prompt or `{"kind":"prompt","text":"..."}`. With EOF alone it uses the chapter's configuration prompt.
+
+One JSON `stream_stats` record reports observed deltas by kind, model-response finalized parts (not tool-result finals), first observed delta milliseconds from request start, elapsed milliseconds, effective streaming, measured usage and the reliable final answer. It prints no thinking content or signatures. Counts are observed, not predicted. Negative first-delta time means no delta was observed, never an invented zero measurement.
+
+`api.log` is a root-serialized diagnostic stream and `CH07_AGENT_LOG` (default `ch07-agent.jsonl`) is durable canonical history. Treat both as private runtime files; do not publish raw logs. Shutdown joins producers before trace closure and summary publication.
